            <ArticleTitle>Pain: Do ACE inhibitors exacerbate complex regional pain syndrome?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>306-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/nrneurol.2009.73</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Complex regional pain syndrome is a chronic condition arising mainly after tissue injury and involves both inflammatory and neurogenic factors. Use of angiotensin-converting-enzyme inhibitors has been associated with an increased risk of developing the chronic pain condition, which suggests possible roles for substance P and bradykinin in the underlying pathogenic process.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
